{
  "analysis": "The review describes a 30-second matchmaking connection delay, but this is a service or matchmaking wait rather than a designed timer that forces the player to play at a scheduled time, so it does not support Playing by Appointment. The review also says that obtaining weapon upgrades and perks requires continuing to battle for wins, implying repeated gameplay to make progress, which supports Grinding. The match battles are competitive encounters, supporting Competition. The claim that rewards are merely for show expresses dissatisfaction with the reward presentation but does not explicitly describe an identified dark-pattern mechanic.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "T_Grinding",
      "span": "Its difficult to get weapon upgrades or any percs others you stick battling to win",
      "rule_applied": "definition",
      "rationale": "The reviewer links obtaining upgrades and perks to continuing battles for wins, implying repetitive gameplay is required for progress."
    },
    {
      "label": "S_Competition",
      "span": "you stick battling to win",
      "rule_applied": "darkpattern.games indicator: “The game makes you compete against other players.”",
      "rationale": "Battling to win in a match describes the player competing against other players."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The review describes a competitive multiplayer battle system in which the player repeatedly faces other players using a narrow set of powerful cards after reaching 8k trophies. It also explicitly describes a pay-to-win design: progressing to higher ranks is portrayed as difficult through skill alone, with spending implied to provide an advantage. The complaints about updates and card buffs express dissatisfaction with balance and do not, by themselves, establish power creep or another separate mechanic.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "S_Competition",
      "span": "all you play against after 8k trophies is mega knight,pekka, and golem",
      "rule_applied": "definition; darkpattern.games indicator: “The game makes you compete against other players.”",
      "rationale": "The span explicitly describes the player competing against other players in matches."
    },
    {
      "label": "M_PayToProgress",
      "span": "its also pay to win and usually doesn't let you get higher from just using skill",
      "rule_applied": "Pay to Win indicator: “Patterns that grant advantages to players who spend money.”",
      "rationale": "The reviewer explicitly characterizes the game as pay to win and links payment-related advantage to reaching higher progression."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The review describes an in-game move-limited mechanic: a game element may fail to appear during 5 original moves plus 5 additional moves, but the text does not establish that this is gambling, a paid progress gate, or repetitive grinding. The reviewer also explicitly refers to buying from the game \"beyond the pass\"; the search resolves this as Fishdom's Gold Pass, which is a battle-pass feature and supports Recurring Fee. Finally, \"trade lives\" describes exchanging in-game resources with friends or teammates, which fits Reciprocity. Merely mentioning friends and a team does not establish friend recruitment rewards or an obligation to keep playing, so Forced Fellowship is not assigned.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "M_RecurringFee",
      "span": "beyond the pass",
      "rule_applied": "Battle passes [indicators]",
      "rationale": "The reviewer identifies an in-game pass that can be purchased; the resolved Fishdom Gold Pass is a battle-pass feature covered by Recurring Fee."
    },
    {
      "label": "S_Reciprocity",
      "span": "Get friends and a team and trade lives.",
      "rule_applied": "Reciprocity indicator: feeling obligated to return a favor, share resources, trade an item, etc.",
      "rationale": "The span describes trading lives, an exchange of in-game resources between players."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": true,
  "search_query": "Fishdom game \"the pass\" diamonds lives team trade lives",
  "search_result": "The search established that Fishdom uses a Gold Pass/season pass, so \"the pass\" refers to a battle-pass feature. ([apps.apple.com](https://apps.apple.com/au/app/fishdom/id664575829?platform=ipad&see-all=reviews&utm_source=openai))"
}

{
  "analysis": "The review describes three active design behaviours. First, the request for a shorter time for a new life implies that lives are replenished through an in-game waiting timer; the requested 5–10 minute duration itself is only a suggestion, not a separate mechanic. Second, the game includes daily prizes that reset when the player misses a day, which both penalizes missed attendance and pressures the player to return daily. The mention of small tasks such as celebrating does not establish repetitive tasks required for progress, so it does not support Grinding.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "T_PlayingByAppointment",
      "span": "maybe only 5-10 minutes for a new life",
      "rule_applied": "Wait to Play: in-game timers that impose an arbitrary wait before play can continue.",
      "rationale": "The request for a shorter time for a new life implies that the existing life system makes the player wait before playing again."
    },
    {
      "label": "T_DailyRewards",
      "span": "just because you miss a day doesnt mean that you need to start over on your daily prizes",
      "rule_applied": "Daily log-in rewards that reset or penalize the player for failing to log in.",
      "rationale": "Daily prizes are tied to daily attendance, and missing a day causes the reward sequence to restart."
    },
    {
      "label": "S_FearOfMissingOutFOMO",
      "span": "just because you miss a day doesnt mean that you need to start over on your daily prizes",
      "rule_applied": "Patterns that cause players to miss rewards or fall behind if they stop playing.",
      "rationale": "Resetting daily-prize progress when a day is missed pressures the player to keep returning so they do not lose progress and rewards."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The review describes an in-game advertisement that cannot be dismissed normally: there is no close control, tapping the ad redirects to the store, and returning to the game leaves the ad blocking gameplay until the app is terminated. This makes the player continue viewing or forcibly exit the advertisement and uses the interface to remove the normal opt-out path. The reviewer does not explicitly attribute the behavior to a bug or technical fault, so the described ad and interface behaviors remain codable.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "T_Advertisement",
      "span": "there is no way to close it. No cross mark on the screen",
      "rule_applied": "definition",
      "rationale": "The advertisement cannot be dismissed, compelling the player to keep viewing it or terminate the game."
    },
    {
      "label": "M_UIMisdirection",
      "span": "if you try to click anywhere on the screen it takes you to store",
      "rule_applied": "definition",
      "rationale": "The ad interface directs taps toward the store while providing no usable opt-out or dismissal path."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The reviewer describes a current consequence of deleting the game: their in-game purchases and accumulated effort would be lost. This makes leaving or uninstalling costly because the player would forfeit value already invested. The request to add persistent saving is a proposed feature, so it is not coded separately. No other current mechanic is explicitly described.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "P_EasyToGetHardToLose",
      "span": "if I deleted the game I would lose everything my in-game purchases and my hard work",
      "rule_applied": "Invested (Endowed) Value; definition",
      "rationale": "The player says that uninstalling would forfeit money spent and progress earned, making accumulated investment harder to abandon."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The review describes empire-building and expansion requiring strategic play, plus real-time battles against other players. The multiplayer combat explicitly places players in competition with one another. The positive tone and claims about graphics, adventure, excitement, and storyline do not independently describe any coded dark-pattern mechanic.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "S_Competition",
      "span": "battling other players in real-time combat",
      "rule_applied": "definition: patterns that make players compete against other players",
      "rationale": "The review explicitly describes real-time combat between the player and other players."
